Notebook[{Cell["Generic Page-reduced radial identity", "Title"], 
  Cell["Version-3 human notation guide (documentation only; no Input cell is \
changed). In the compact solution and verifier notebooks: x=r^2; q1,q2,q3 are \
the harmonic parameters mu1,mu2,mu3, not normalized conserved charges; jrot \
is the rotation parameter j; U1,U2,U3 are the electric corrections delta u_I; \
B1,B2,B3 are the gauge-covariant fibre corrections; Om is delta omega; Ft, \
Gr, and Sq are the temporal warp, radial warp, and squashing corrections; P \
and S are delta p and delta s, where X1=exp(2p/3-s), X2=exp(2p/3+s), and \
X3=exp(-4p/3). Physical quantities are Q_I=Pi mu_I/(4 G5) and J1=J2=Pi j/(4 \
G5). See the report section 'Human-readable notation and result at a glance' \
for the full dictionary.", "Text"], 
  Cell["Exact in rotation, plus an independent O(j^2) unreduced check", 
   "Subtitle"], Cell["This standalone notebook embeds the original radial \
equation, all three Page rules, the stored algebraic radial coefficient, the \
O(j^2) unreduced radial equation and Page rules, and the closed O(j^2) \
solution. It reads no external file.", "Text"], 
  Cell["The general proof first decomposes the raw radial equation in the \
three electric jets, substitutes the Page rules, proves linearity in Gr, \
reconstructs the algebraic rule, matches the stored coefficient, and proves \
that its denominator and endpoint polynomials keep the coefficient nonzero in \
the physical exterior. The O(j^2) proof then substitutes the closed solution \
directly into the original unreduced equation.", "Text"], 
  Cell["1. Embedded equation archive", "Section"], 
  Cell[BoxData["ClearAll[\"Global`*\"]; $HistoryLength=0; \
$RecursionLimit=300000; $MaxExtraPrecision=10000;"], "Input"], 
  Cell[BoxData["inputData=<|\"homGr\" -> (-6*jrot*q1^2*q2*q3*B1[x] - \
